      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Incident: {{ $('Normalize Alert').first().json.id }}\nAlert: {{ JSON.stringify($('Normalize Alert').first().json.raw) }}\nTriage: {{ JSON.stringify($('Parse Triage').first().json) }}\nGitHub repo: owner `{{ $env.GITHUB_REPO.split('/')[0] }}`, repo `{{ $env.GITHUB_REPO.split('/')[1] }}`, branch `main`. The backend code lives under `backend/`.",
        "hasOutputParser": false,
        "needsFallback": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are the Investigator agent. Collect evidence; do not fix anything. Use at most 4 tool calls:\n1. get_recent_logs with level=\"error\" and limit=20 to get the error and stack trace.\n2. get_deploy_history with limit=5 to see recent commits (each commit is a deploy).\n3. get_commit (GitHub) on the newest commit(s) to read the diff, only if needed to confirm.\nThe suspect commit is the one whose diff touches the file/function in the stack trace. The last good commit is the commit right before the suspect.\nRules: never guess. If the logs contain no error entries, or no commit diff matches the stack trace, set evidence_found=false, leave suspect_commit and last_good_commit as null, and explain why in evidence. If the alert comes from CI/CD (source \"ci-cd\"): `commit` is the commit that was just deployed (prime suspect), `previous_sha` is the commit that was live before it (the last good commit unless evidence says otherwise), and failed_checks are the smoke-test failures. Read the diff of `commit` with get_commit.\nOnly set evidence_found=true when real errors (error log lines or failed CI smoke checks) AND a matching commit diff support it.\n\nAnswer with ONLY one JSON object, no prose, no code fences:\n{\"evidence_found\":true,\"error_signature\":\"<error message>\",\"stack_top\":\"<file:line function>\",\"suspect_commit\":{\"sha\":\"<full sha>\",\"message\":\"...\",\"files\":[\"backend/...\"]},\"last_good_commit\":{\"sha\":\"<full sha>\",\"message\":\"...\"},\"file_path\":\"backend/src/<file>.js\",\"evidence\":[\"<short fact>\",\"...\"],\"confidence\":0.0}",
          "maxIterations": 8,
          "enableStreaming": false
        }
      }
    },
